From: SM-G955N Ubuntu port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] hooks: resolve Android MB_CUR_MAX through host libc

Android 9 libc++ imports __ctype_get_mb_cur_max. The stock Bionic function
uses its pthread TLS layout, which differs from glibc. Match the existing
locale hooks and use the host libc implementation with the same size_t(void)
ABI, rather than entering Bionic TLS or returning a hardcoded locale value.

diff --git a/hybris/common/hooks.c b/hybris/common/hooks.c
--- a/hybris/common/hooks.c
+++ b/hybris/common/hooks.c
@@ -3314,6 +3314,8 @@
     HOOK_DIRECT(uselocale),
     HOOK_DIRECT(localeconv),
     HOOK_DIRECT(setlocale),
+    /* Bionic uses incompatible pthread TLS to implement MB_CUR_MAX. */
+    HOOK_DIRECT_NO_DEBUG(__ctype_get_mb_cur_max),
     /* sys/mman.h */
 #if defined(LP64)
     HOOK_DIRECT(mmap),
